(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[3 1 "// Generators (doc/python/PYI-SPEC.md §7.4-§7.5; the survey's PYS7 (a); PY5d): a generator, a"] [4 1 "// coroutine and an async generator are the frame of their function's call kept between resumptions."] [5 1 "// The call makes the object without running the frame (newGeneratorHook); each resumption runs the"] [6 1 "// kept frame by (*Thread).run as an entry frame, a yield (yield-value, or yield-from delegating)"] [7 1 "// returns from the loop with Frame.Suspended set, and the frame's handler table sees an exception"] [8 1 "// thrown in at the instruction it is suspended at (Lasti). CPython's Objects/genobject.c and the"] [9 1 "// YIELD_VALUE, SEND and RETURN_GENERATOR parts of Python/bytecodes.c."] [26 1 "// Generator is a generator, a coroutine or an async generator (CPython's PyGenObject, PyCoroObject"] [27 1 "// and PyAsyncGenObject): the kept frame of its function's call."] [30 18 "// nil once finished (gi_frame None)"] [32 18 "// __name__, the function's"] [33 18 "// __qualname__"] [34 18 "// run at least once (FRAME_CREATED otherwise)"] [35 18 "// gi_running"] [36 2 "// handled is the exception the frame is handling while it is suspended (gi_exc_state), nil when none."] [38 2 "// origin is cr_origin: the frames that created a coroutine while origin tracking was on, nil otherwise"] [40 2 "// the async generator's state (PyAsyncGenObject)"] [41 20 "// ag_closed"] [42 20 "// ag_running_async: an asend or athrow awaits it"] [43 20 "// ag_hooks_inited: sys's firstiter hook called (PY6h's REQUEST, queue 200)"] [56 1 "// newGenerator is a call's object of a function whose code is a generator's, a coroutine's or an"] [57 1 "// async generator's: f bound, not run."] [75 1 "// genThrow is an exception thrown into a suspended frame: the resumption runs the frame's"] [76 1 "// yield-value or yield-from again (its PC set back to Lasti), which finds it here and raises it"] [77 1 "// there (yield-from first throws it into its delegate), so the frame's handlers see it at the"] [78 1 "// suspension point. One thread runs at a time, and the frame's first instruction run is that one."] [82 20 "// a GeneratorExit closes the delegate (false: aclose's, thrown into it)"] [85 1 "// genSuspendedAt is the operation f is suspended at, when it is."] [93 1 "// yieldFrom is the delegate the generator is suspended in (gi_yieldfrom), or nil."] [101 1 "// resume runs g with v sent into it (exc nil) or exc thrown into it (gen_send_ex2): the value it"] [102 1 "// yields (yielded non-nil), or the value it returns (returned, the generator finished), or what it"] [103 1 "// raises (err; a StopIteration raised in it is a RuntimeError, PEP 479)."] [112 4 "// throw() into an exhausted coroutine is a reuse (gen_send_ex2), close()'s GeneratorExit is not"] [125 4 "// thrown into a generator not started: raised at its start, it finishes"] [141 2 "// the generator's own exception slot over the resuming level's (gi_exc_state pushed on the exc_info stack)"] [171 1 "// stopIterationError is PEP 479's RuntimeError for a StopIteration (or, in an async generator, a"] [172 1 "// StopAsyncIteration) raised out of g's frame: its cause and context the exception, its traceback g's"] [173 1 "// frame's entry (CPython raises it in the frame, INTRINSIC_STOPITERATION_ERROR)."] [197 1 "// newStopIteration is StopIteration(v), with no arguments when v is None (gen_send_ex's)."] [205 1 "// stopIterationValue is a raised StopIteration's value (_PyGen_FetchStopIterationValue), ok false when"] [206 1 "// err is not one."] [218 1 "// isRaised is err a raised exception of type typ (or a subtype)."] [224 1 "// send is g.send(v): what it yields, or StopIteration with what it returns."] [236 1 "// throw is g.throw(exc), exc already an exception."] [248 1 "// close is g.close() (gen_close): GeneratorExit thrown in; its return value when it returns."] [270 1 "// throwArgs is throw's arguments as the exception to raise (_gen_throw's normalization): an"] [271 1 "// instance, or a class called with the value (none, an instance of it, a tuple of arguments, or the"] [272 1 "// one argument). The (type, value, traceback) signature is deprecated, not refused."] [313 1 "// genSendTo is a send into an iterator delegated to (SEND): a generator's or coroutine's resume, else"] [314 1 "// __next__ when v is None, else its send method; yielded non-nil, or the value it returned (a"] [315 1 "// StopIteration's, or None at an iterator's end)."] [341 1 "// genThrowTo throws exc into a delegate (_gen_throw's yf part): a GeneratorExit closes it (when"] [342 1 "// closeOnGenEx) and is raised in the delegating frame; else its throw, when it has one (handled false:"] [343 1 "// raise exc in the delegating frame)."] [372 1 "// genCloseIter closes a delegate (gen_close_iter): a generator's or coroutine's close, else its close"] [373 1 "// method when it has one."] [390 1 "// asyncGenWrapped is a value an async generator yields (CPython's _PyAsyncGenWrappedValue): its asend"] [391 1 "// and athrow see it apart from the values its awaits yield to the event loop."] [396 1 "// opYieldValue is yield-value: the value popped and yielded (wrapped in an async generator), f kept"] [397 1 "// suspended; resumed, the value sent is on the stack (pushed by resume), or an exception thrown in is"] [398 1 "// raised here."] [413 1 "// opYieldFrom is yield-from ([receiver value] -> its return value): CPython's SEND, YIELD_VALUE and"] [414 1 "// END_SEND loop as one operation. Each value the receiver yields suspends f with the instruction run"] [415 1 "// again on resumption (PC set back to it), the receiver kept below and the sent value pushed on it."] [422 11 "// the placeholder resume pushed"] [445 1 "// opGetYieldFromIter is get-yield-from-iter: a generator or a coroutine as it is (a coroutine only in a"] [446 1 "// coroutine's code), else iter(o)."] [465 1 "// genMethods are the methods of the types of PY5d's files, put into their dictionaries by d5Ready"] [466 1 "// (lazily: a dictionary's keys need str's hash, which str.go's init sets after these files' inits)."] [473 1 "// d5Method declares a method of a type of PY5d's: name in t's dictionary as a built-in method."] [484 1 "// d5Ready fills the dictionaries of PY5d's types with their methods, once (each of their GetAttr"] [485 1 "// slots and operations calls it first)."] [506 1 "// d5GetAttr is the GetAttr slot of PY5d's types: their methods ready, then extra (attributes not in"] [507 1 "// the dictionary), then object's lookup."] [520 1 "// d5Args checks a method's argument count: between min and max positional, no keywords."] [536 1 "// coroOriginDepth is sys.set_coroutine_origin_tracking_depth's depth (0: off)."] [539 1 "// coroOrigin is compute_cr_origin: (filename, lineno, function name) of the creating frame and up to depth-1 of its"] [540 1 "// callers, innermost first."] [556 1 "// genRepr is \"<KIND object QUALNAME at 0x...>\", the address an identity number."] [563 1 "// genAttrs are the attributes a generator, coroutine or async generator answers outside its"] [564 1 "// dictionary (prefix gi_, cr_ or ag_)."] [616 2 "// Next ends without the return value: the loop's for-iter and the abstract Next do not clear a"] [617 2 "// raised StopIteration yet (asked of PY5b and PY5c); __next__ and send raise it with the value."] [634 1 "// d5GenMethods declares send, throw and close of a generator or a coroutine."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[63 61] [95 38] [190 26] [290 32] [294 30] [317 31] [325 44] [330 38] [346 31] [351 31] [364 38] [375 31] [449 28] [512 35] [544 18] [544 50] [547 54] [596 25] [623 62] [637 54] [653 55]]} (go/file "gen.go" :imports [])

;; Generators (doc/python/PYI-SPEC.md §7.4-§7.5; the survey's PYS7 (a); PY5d): a generator, a
;; coroutine and an async generator are the frame of their function's call kept between resumptions.
;; The call makes the object without running the frame (newGeneratorHook); each resumption runs the
;; kept frame by (*Thread).run as an entry frame, a yield (yield-value, or yield-from delegating)
;; returns from the loop with Frame.Suspended set, and the frame's handler table sees an exception
;; thrown in at the instruction it is suspended at (Lasti). CPython's Objects/genobject.c and the
;; YIELD_VALUE, SEND and RETURN_GENERATOR parts of Python/bytecodes.c.

